# Test: the looking glass serves TLS when no tls leaf is written
# VALIDATES: spec-fixit-mgmt-listener-auth-guard AC-5 -- the looking-glass TLS
# default is ON, and the documented `tls false` opt-out still serves plaintext.
# The raw config tree carries no YANG defaults, so an absent leaf is simply
# missing and the extractor must read it as true; flipping only the YANG default
# would change nothing that reaches the daemon. `ze init` runs first because TLS
# certificates live in blob storage, so this exercises the shipped path rather
# than the no-storage fallback.
# PREVENTS: a looking glass publishing route data and session state in the clear
# because the operator wrote no tls leaf, and the opposite regression where the
# opt-out stops being honored and a plaintext consumer breaks with no recourse.

option=timeout:value=60s


cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-test fixture plugin/lg-tls-default-on:timeout=60s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=OK: looking glass defaults to TLS
expect=stderr:contains=OK: TLS handshake completed and the API answered
expect=stderr:contains=OK: the tls false opt-out is honored
